    {
      "id": "HS-RED2-F01",
      "severity": "material",
      "classification": "confirmed static fixture task-lifetime defect; no runtime executed",
      "path": "BookOfEternityClient.IntegrationTests/GameEngineTurnLifecycleTests.HotSubmissionReadyDrift.cs",
      "source": "f71c3984355c70cc81f73f52cdb7007ff193edd8",
      "lines": [
        124,
        151
      ],
      "title": "Publisher and real Wait are not jointly owned on failure",
      "scenario": "The GM Task.Run asserts its ten-second deadline or faults before publishing Ready, but the fixture is awaiting only WaitForContractRepairAsync with an empty QueuedConsoleInputSource. That production wait has no finite exit without a signal/input and does not observe the publisher failure. Conversely, a real Wait exception bypasses await gmRepair and permits participation/root cleanup while that task still polls or publishes.",
      "consequence": "A setup/IO failure can turn into category timeout instead of a promptly reported causal failure; the publisher can outlive its fixture operation and race strict root cleanup. Successful-path await and category process cleanup do not establish task quiescence on these exits.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "path": "BookOfEternityClient.IntegrationTests/GameEngineTurnLifecycleTests.HotSubmissionReadyDrift.cs",
          "start": 89,
          "end": 90
        },
        {
          "path": "BookOfEternityClient.IntegrationTests/GameEngineTurnLifecycleTests.HotSubmissionReadyDrift.cs",
          "start": 124,
          "end": 151
        },
        {
          "path": "BookOfEternityClient/Core/GameEngine/GameEngine.ValidationAndRepair.cs",
          "start": 3363,
          "end": 3429
        },
        {
          "path": "BookOfEternityClient.IntegrationTests/GameEngineTurnLifecycleTests.cs",
          "start": 11073,
          "end": 11098
        },
        {
          "path": "BookOfEternityClient.IntegrationTests/CleanupPublicationCut.cs",
          "start": 131,
          "end": 144
        }
      ],
      "requirement": "Own and await all GM/input/cleanup work before participation/root disposal; retain first unexpected failure and strict cleanup rather than relying on category timeout. The focused consultation explicitly requires awaiting these tasks.",
      "correction": "Retain the existing queued input instance; coordinate both real tasks. On publisher failure request the real Wait cancellation through the existing Escape input seam, observe/await its completion, and preserve the publisher error. On Wait completion/failure cancel polling and await the publisher in a finally path before operation/root teardown; do not swallow publication/cleanup errors or leave a running task after a timeout wrapper. Ensure the ordinary success path and Ready\u2192manifest cut remain unchanged. No production hook, synthetic lease, authority or close substitute is needed."
    }
  ],
